  "full_response": "Certainly! Below is an outline for a training slide deck aimed at educating employees about protecting classified and confidential materials in the workplace. This outline includes key sections and topics that should be covered.\n\n---\n\n### Slide Deck Outline: Protecting Classified and Confidential Materials\n\n#### Slide 1: Title Slide\n- **Title:** Protecting Classified and Confidential Materials in the Workplace\n- **Subtitle:** A Guide for Secure Handling and Storage\n- **Presented by:** [Your Name], [Your Position]\n- **Date**\n\n---\n\n#### Slide 2: Introduction\n- **Overview of Confidentiality**\n  - Importance of protecting sensitive information\n  - Potential consequences of data breaches\n- **Objective of the Training**\n  - Equip employees with knowledge and tools to safeguard classified and confidential materials\n\n---\n\n#### Slide 3: Understanding Information Sensitivity\n- **Definitions**\n  - CLASSIFIED_DATA: Information with national security implications\n  - CONFIDENTIAL: Information that requires protection but is less sensitive than classified data\n- **Classifications**\n  - Explanation of data classifications (e.g., Top Secret, Secret, Confidential, Unclassified)\n\n---\n\n#### Slide 4: Policies and Legal Requirements\n- **Relevant Policies**\n  - Overview of company policies regarding data protection\n- **Legal Framework**\n  - Relevant laws and regulations (e.g., GDPR, HIPAA, FISMA)\n  \n---\n\n#### Slide 5: Identifying Classified and Confidential Information\n- **Signs and Markings**\n  - How to identify classified/confidential documents and materials\n- **Common Sources**\n  - Departments and roles that handle sensitive information\n\n---\n\n#### Slide 6: Access Control\n- **Need-to-Know Basis**\n  - Ensuring only authorized personnel access sensitive information\n- **Access Control Systems**\n  - Physical and digital access controls (e.g., key cards, passwords, biometrics)\n\n---\n\n#### Slide 7: Secure Handling and Transmission\n- **Handling Sensitive Materials**\n  - Best practices for handling physical documents (e.g., locked cabinets)\n- **Secure Communication**\n  - Using encrypted emails, secure messaging apps, and VPNs\n\n---\n\n#### Slide 8: Storage and Disposal\n- **Secure Storage**\n  - Safe storage solutions and protocols\n- **Proper Disposal**\n  - Shredding documents, secure deletion of digital files\n\n---\n\n#### Slide 9: Incident Response\n- **Recognizing Breaches**\n  - Signs of a data breach or information leak\n- **Reporting Mechanisms**\n  - Steps to",
